---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Monogram from '../components/Monogram.astro';
import Wordmark from '../components/Wordmark.astro';
import Equation from '../components/Equation.astro';
import QuestionBlock from '../components/QuestionBlock.astro';
import { researchQuestions } from '../data/questions';
---

<Page
  title="About"
  description="Alan Chester · researcher, scholar, engineer. Studying observation representations in long-horizon RL, agentic system design, and multi-agent trust."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-prose px-6 pt-16 pb-24">
    <header class="flex flex-col items-start gap-4">
      <Monogram size="lg" />
      <Wordmark as="h1" size="lg" />
      <Equation size="md" />
    </header>

    <section class="mt-12">
      <p class="eyebrow">Research focus</p>
      <div class="mt-5 space-y-5 text-lg leading-[1.7] text-graphite dark:text-mist">
        <p>
          I work at the intersection of cloud infrastructure, agentic AI
          systems, reinforcement learning, and multi-agent trust. The site you
          are reading is where the research and technical work lives. Notes
          from the bench.
        </p>
        <p>
          The active empirical work: in long-horizon reinforcement learning,
          do symbolic observations beat pixel observations once encoder
          capacity is properly controlled? Pokémon Red is the environment,
          RecurrentPPO via SB3-Contrib the method.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-16 border-t border-mist pt-10 dark:border-graphite">
      <p class="eyebrow">Current questions</p>
      <div class="mt-8">
        {researchQuestions.map((q) => (
          <QuestionBlock topic={q.topic} question={q.question} method={q.method} />
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-16 border-t border-mist pt-10 dark:border-graphite">
      <p class="eyebrow">Currently</p>
      <ul class="mt-5 space-y-3 text-graphite dark:text-mist">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <span class="mt-0.5 inline-block w-4 shrink-0 font-sans text-base font-bold leading-none text-accent" aria-hidden="true">ε</span>
          <span>Studying observation representations in long-horizon RL. Pixel vs. symbolic vs. hybrid, under capacity-matched encoders.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <span class="mt-0.5 inline-block w-4 shrink-0 font-sans text-base font-bold leading-none text-accent" aria-hidden="true">ε</span>
          <span>Researching team architectures and trust topology for human-AI systems.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <span class="mt-0.5 inline-block w-4 shrink-0 font-sans text-base font-bold leading-none text-accent" aria-hidden="true">ε</span>
          <span>MBA candidate, NC State Jenkins Graduate School of Management.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-16 border-t border-mist pt-10 dark:border-graphite">
      <p class="eyebrow">Background</p>
      <div class="mt-5 space-y-5 text-graphite dark:text-mist">
        <p>
          About fifteen years across kernel engineering, Kubernetes platform
          development, cloud security, and product leadership.
        </p>
        <p>
          Dual <span class="font-mono">B.S.</span> in Computer Science and
          Applied Mathematics, NC State. CS gave me the discipline to ship
          systems that run in production. Applied Math gave me the internals
          of the models the rest of the field is now using. Security taught
          me to see the risk others miss. The MBA in progress is the habit of
          proving ROI rather than asserting it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-16 border-t border-mist pt-10 dark:border-graphite">
      <p class="eyebrow">Philosophy</p>
      <div class="mt-5 text-lg leading-[1.7] text-graphite dark:text-mist">
        <p>
          The brand is borrowed from real analysis. <span class="equation">ε</span> is
          whatever the world demands. Uptime, accuracy, security, ROI.
          <span class="equation">δ</span> is the move that meets it. Data points
          the gradient.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-16 border-t border-mist pt-10 dark:border-graphite">
      <p class="eyebrow">Connect</p>
      <ul class="mt-5 space-y-2 font-mono text-sm">
        <li>
          <a href="mailto:amcheste@gmail.com" class="text-muted no-underline hover:text-accent">
            amcheste@gmail.com
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/alan-chester-8757b98b/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-muted no-underline hover:text-accent"
          >linkedin.com/in/alan-chester-8757b98b</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/amcheste"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-muted no-underline hover:text-accent"
          >github.com/amcheste</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://x.com/amcheste"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-muted no-underline hover:text-accent"
          >x: @amcheste</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>
</Page>
